                    "fillColorRefFile": "a877156d-2168-8112-8008-dc507254add2"
                  }
                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "The value and its unit live together in the box, because paramValueText hands them over as a single string \u2014 \"-6.0 dB\", \"Lowpass\", \"1\/4 dotted\". Splitting them would mean parsing the plugin's own formatting apart. When a plugin offers no text, the tile falls back to the numeric value plus the separate unit field; when it does, the unit slot simply goes unused, as on KNEE = \"soft\"."
              }
